 ## 5. Git and GitHub: nothing converts
 
-- **The root `.gitattributes` says one thing: `* -text`.** Git then never changes a line ending, in either
-  direction, on any PC, whatever its own `core.autocrlf` setting is. The existing special lines are no longer
-  needed.
-- **It does not reach `GAIS\`, and this standard says so** (EX_303 FFS-C03; the owner assented: section 8 item
-  6). That folder is another project's. It has two attribute files of its own
-  (`GAIS/OUTLANDISH_01/.gitattributes`, `GAIS/OUTLANDISH_01/OUTLANDISH_WSL/.gitattributes`), which Git obeys for the
-  paths under them, and the second tells Git to convert that project's `.py`, `.sh`, `.md` and `.bat` files.
-  Claude never writes under `GAIS\`. So the true statement is: **Git converts nothing anywhere in this project;
-  under `GAIS\` that other project's own rules stay as they are.** The repository holds no other attribute file.
+- **The root `.gitattributes` holds three lines** (v0.2; the owner, section 8 item 7):
